# HR Analytics Dashboard – Employee Attrition Analysis

## Project Overview
This project explores employee attrition and workforce patterns using an HR dataset and an interactive HR Analytics Dashboard.

## Objectives
- Monitor employee headcount, active employees and attrition.
- Compare attrition across departments and gender.
- Explore attrition patterns by age group and education field.
- Review job satisfaction ratings by job role.
- Present HR insights to support further investigation and retention planning.

## Tools
- Microsoft Excel (source data review)
- Tableau for visialisation

## Dataset Summary
- Employee records: 1,470
- Fields: 41
- Attrition: 237 employees
- Active employees: 1,233
- Overall attrition rate: 16.12%
- Average age: 37 years

## Key Findings
- Sales has the highest department attrition rate in the dataset.
- Employees under 25 have the highest age-band attrition rate.
- The dataset records 150 male exits and 87 female exits.
- Life Sciences has the highest number of exits by education field.
- Job satisfaction ratings are compared across job roles.

## Conclusion
The dashboard provides a descriptive overview of employee attrition and highlights groups for further HR investigation. The patterns are not proof of the causes of attrition.

